    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28195" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">matĕris</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">matăris</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">madăris</span></b> ), is, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">matăra</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		Celtic, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Celtic javelin, pike</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nonnulli inter carros rotasque mataras ac
					tragulas subiciebant nostrosque vulnerabant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 1, 26, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">humero matari trajecto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					7, 24, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">materis Transalpina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 4, 32, 43</span></i>
			: Galli materibus configunt, Sisenn. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Non. 556, 8</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">id. ib. 9</span></i>.</div>
